  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 252 PM CST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nIt may sound like a broken record, but we are warm and dry again\ntoday, with the next cold front bringing mostly a change in\ntemperatures. The disturbance along the Gulf Coast and associated\nupper-level trough will be lifting across the Southeastern CONUS\nthis weekend. The northern jet stream will remain progressive\nthrough the end of next week, and the southern jet will translate\nfrom the Pacific and along the Gulf Coast before weakening. The\nconfidence in timing of waves under such a pattern is low, but the\ngreater chances are for our forecast area to remain dry after the\nSunday/Monday cold front passage. Some model runs have generated\nsome rain in far eastern Mississippi around mid week with the next\nwave, but better chances are focused east of our area.\nTemperatures will fall closer to normal in the wake of the cold\nfront and then begin a gradual warming trend. /NF/",
